title: NCI Plot
keyword: NCIPLOT
manual: nciplot/
cite: nci_2010 nci_2012

Makes a non-covalent interactions (NCI) plot: the reduced density gradient (RDG, s) and the
signed density sign(λ2)ρ (the density times the sign of the second eigenvalue of its
Hessian) are calculated on a grid, and the isosurfaces of the former are drawn colored by
the latter. Low-RDG regions at low density mark non-covalent interactions: negative sign(λ2)ρ
(blue) for attractive contacts, near zero (green) for van der Waals contacts and positive
(red) for steric repulsion.

# Options

- "Density": the "Field" the plot is calculated from (the promolecular density if the system
  has no fields). For a grid field, "Derivatives" are calculated from the interpolant or by
  Fourier transform.
- "Region" and "Grid": the region the grid spans and the grid "Level" (coarse to very fine,
  or custom). "Estimate Cost" predicts the time.
- "Fragments": the molecules of the system and the fragments added with "Add from
  Selection" (the atoms selected in the view). With two or more fragments selected, only the
  regions between them are plotted: a point is kept if no single fragment contributes more
  than "Dominance" of the promolecular density of the fragments, and the fragments together
  at least "Share" of that of the whole system. "Show region" draws that region in the view.
- "Plot": the "Isovalue (s)" of the RDG isosurface, the "sign(λ2)ρ range (a.u.)" outside
  which points are left out, and the "Color scale (a.u.)" of the isosurface. More: "Voids
  only" plots only where the promolecular density is below "Void density (a.u.)".
- "Output": "Complete molecules" completes the molecules that cross the cell boundary in
  the xyz file written with the cubes.

# Results

"Calculate" evaluates the grids, loads them as two fields and adds an isosurface object
"NCI plot" with its color bar to the view. The "Plot" section shows the
scatter of s against sign(λ2)ρ; drag its lines to change the isovalue, the range and the
color scale. "Domains" lists the connected regions under the isovalue with their volume and
electrons. "Write Files..." writes the cube files of the NCIPLOT keyword and "Save Plot..."
the scatter plot as a PNG image.
